<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikolai Bobrikov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1839">1839</a>–<a href="/years/1904">1904</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikolai Bobrikov was a Russian general who served as Governor-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> from 1898. He drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russification">Russification</a> of the grand duchy, imposing the February Manifesto of 1899, which allowed imperial laws to override Finnish ones, the language manifesto of 1900 and a conscription law of 1901. He was shot in Helsinki in June 1904 by the Finnish official Eugen Schauman.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikolai-bobrikov.jpg" alt="Nikolai Bobrikov" width="261" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nikolai_Bobrikov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
